    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the probability that a randomly selected point \\((x, y, z)\\) within the cube defined by \\(-1 \\leq x \\leq 1\\), \\(-1 \\leq y \\leq 1\\), and \\(-1 \\leq z \\leq 1\\) lies within the sphere defined by \\(x^2 + y^2 + z^2 \\leq 1\\).\n\n### Step-by-Step Solution:\n\n1. **Volume of the Cube:**\n   The cube has side length 2 (from -1 to 1), so its volume is:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{cube}} = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 = 8\n   \\]\n\n2. **Volume of the Sphere:**\n   The sphere has a radius of 1 (since \\(x^2 + y^2 + z^2 \\leq 1\\)), so its volume is:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{sphere}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (1)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi\n   \\]\n\n3. **Probability Calculation:**\n   The probability that a randomly selected point \\((x, y, z)\\) lies within the sphere is the ratio of the volume of the sphere to the volume of the cube:\n   \\[\n   P = \\frac{V_{\\text{sphere}}}{V_{\\text{cube}}} = \\frac{\\frac{4}{3} \\pi}{8} = \\frac{4 \\pi}{24} = \\frac{\\pi}{6}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the probability that \\(x^2 + y^2 + z^2 \\leq 1\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}\\).",
