      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "To find the probability that a randomly selected point \\((x, y, z)\\) within the cube \\([-1, 1] \\times [-1, 1] \\times [-1, 1]\\) lies within the sphere \\(x^2 + y^2 + z^2 \\leq 1\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the volume of the cube:**\n   The cube has side length 2 (from -1 to 1 in each dimension). Therefore, the volume of the cube is:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{cube}} = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 = 8\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the volume of the sphere:**\n   The sphere has a radius of 1. The volume \\(V_{\\text{sphere}}\\) of a sphere is given by the formula:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{sphere}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3\n   \\]\n   Substituting \\(r = 1\\):\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{sphere}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (1)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the probability:**\n   The probability \\(P\\) that a randomly selected point in the cube lies within the sphere is the ratio of the volume of the sphere to the volume of the cube:\n   \\[\n   P = \\frac{V_{\\text{sphere}}}{V_{\\text{cube}}} = \\frac{\\frac{4}{3} \\pi}{8} = \\frac{4 \\pi}{3 \\times 8} = \\frac{\\pi}{6}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the probability that a randomly selected point \\((x, y, z)\\) within the cube \\([-1, 1] \\times [-1, 1] \\times [-1, 1]\\) lies within the sphere \\(x^2 + y^2 + z^2 \\leq 1\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}\n\\]",
